# Cloudflare Pages serves an exact static file match before evaluating these
# rules, so the prerendered routes (/, /about, /privacy, /terms, /advertise)
# never hit this file at all - they have a real dist/<route>/index.html.
#
# Cloudflare Pages only supports 200 (rewrite) and 30x (redirect) here - NOT
# 404, unlike Netlify. So the lines below whitelist known client-routed SPA
# pages with a real 200. Anything NOT listed here falls through to
# dist/404.html (written by scripts/prerender.mjs) for a genuine 404 status.
# Truegle's own router still renders its <NotFound /> page either way; only
# the HTTP status differs.
#
# Targets point at /_index.html (a plain copy of index.html), NOT /index.html:
# Cloudflare Pages' default html_handling auto-redirects (308) any resolved
# index.html back to '/', and separately false-positives wildcard rules
# targeting it as an "infinite loop" and silently drops them. Both bugs are
# keyed on the literal filename "index.html", so a differently-named copy
# sidesteps them. See github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11824.

/search           /_index.html  200
/search/*         /_index.html  200
/green            /_index.html  200
/feeling-biased   /_index.html  200
/biased           /_index.html  200
/osint            /_index.html  200
/osint/*          /_index.html  200
/search-portal    /_index.html  200
/search-results   /_index.html  200
/results          /_index.html  200
/auth/*           /_index.html  200
/onboarding       /_index.html  200
/settings         /_index.html  200
/rewards          /_index.html  200
